.\" The package's man page. Every flag in main.go must be listed under OPTIONS:
.\" TestManPageListsEveryFlag checks.
.TH SSL-VISION-PROCESSOR-GUI 1 "" "ssl-vision-processor-gui" "RoboCup SSL"
.SH NAME
ssl-vision-processor-gui \- browser interface for the RoboCup SSL vision_processor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssl-vision-processor-gui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ssl-vision-processor-gui
sets up and runs vision_processor, the Small Size League's shared vision
system. It holds the field geometry and camera settings, locks in camera
calibrations, shows live video and the live field, and publishes the field
geometry on the vision multicast group. Open the address it prints in a
browser.
.PP
With no options it keeps everything in the current user's config and state
folders, creating a default configuration on the first run. A new
configuration publishes nothing until it has been saved once.
.PP
The full guide, including network setup and troubleshooting, is in
.I /usr/share/doc/ssl-vision-processor-gui/README.md
and printed by
.BR \-readme .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-address " host:port"
Address and port for the GUI and its API. Default
.BR :8085 ,
every interface;
.B 127.0.0.1:8085
allows this machine only.
.TP
.BI \-configDir " dir"
The config folder, holding every config file, created if missing. Default
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rcssl/vision-processor-gui ,
or
.I ~/.config/rcssl/vision-processor-gui
without it.
.TP
.BI \-configFile " name"
The configuration to use, a file name in the config folder, created if
missing. Default
.BR vision.yml .
.TP
.BI \-logFile " path"
Rotating log file, written alongside stderr. An empty value turns it off.
Default
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/rcssl/vision-processor-gui/logs/vision-processor-gui.log ,
or under
.I ~/.local/state
without it.
.TP
.BI \-imgDir " dir"
Where vision_processor's debug snapshot images are. Default
.I img
in the same state folder.
.TP
.B \-runCameras
Run every camera's vision_processor on this machine, using the
.B vision_processor
on
.BR PATH ,
and restart it when a setting it reads only at startup changes. Each camera
gets a config file,
.IR cam<id>.yml ,
if it has none. Without it, vision_processors run separately.
.TP
.BI \-logLevel " level"
.BR Debug ,
.BR Info ,
.BR Warn ,
or
.BR Error .
Default
.BR Info .
.TP
.BI \-allowOrigin " origins"
Comma-separated origins (scheme://host:port) whose web pages may use the API
on a competition field, besides the GUI's own;
.B *
for any.
.TP
.BI \-allowHost " names"
Comma-separated extra names this machine is reached by, such as a DNS alias;
.B *
turns the check off.
.TP
.BI \-openapi " path"
Write the API's OpenAPI spec to
.I path
and exit.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-readme
Print the user guide and exit.
.SH SYSTEM SERVICE
The package can run the GUI as the system service
.BR ssl-vision-processor-gui.service ,
as the
.B rcssl-vp-gui
user in the
.B rcssl
group, with its config folder in
.I /var/lib/rcssl/vision-processor-gui
and its log in the journal. Whether it runs, and who can reach it, are the
package's setup questions:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo dpkg-reconfigure ssl-vision-processor-gui
.RE
.PP
Without the system service, the same unit can run as a user service:
.PP
.RS
.B systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now ssl-vision-processor-gui
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/ssl-vision-processor-gui
The system service's
.B ADDRESS
and extra options,
.BR ARGS .
Restart the service after editing.
.TP
.I /var/lib/rcssl/vision-processor-gui
The system service's config folder.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/ssl-vision-processor-gui.service
The system service. Upgrades replace it; customize with
.BR "systemctl edit" .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysctl.d/60-rcssl-multicast.conf
Raises
.B net.core.rmem_max
for live video.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
.TQ
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Replace
.I ~/.config
and
.I ~/.local/state
in the default locations.
.TP
.B PATH
Where
.B \-runCameras
finds vision_processor.
.SH SECURITY
The GUI has no login. Anyone who can reach its port can change the running
configuration and overwrite files in the config folder, including locked
calibrations. Run it only on a network you trust, or allow this machine only
with
.BR "\-address 127.0.0.1:8085" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5),
.BR dpkg-reconfigure (8)
.PP
https://github.com/RoboCup-SSL/ssl-vision-processor
